      "content": "i get not wanting to do it without supervision but it's such a hassle to get another appointment just to ask for a dose change when he's clearly struggling right now. if i just gave him 320mg once or maybe twice this week to get him back on his feet while we wait for an appointment, would that really be a major risk? it feels like we're choosing to let him stay exhausted and weak just to avoid some potential stomach ache. wouldn't a little bit of extra iron be a fair trade-off to get him feeling human again?",
